{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1533066545,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDYzMzMwNDQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2721","origin":"github"},"title":"wishlist: Disable repeated entry of \"hidden\" values","message":"#### What is the problem?\nATM (since f7e0536685806b2de1c95216cc7eb9b2e26bc4f0) regardless of the purpose (e.g. to define new value or just provide a value for an existing one) hidden entries asked to be entered twice.\n\nIMHO this is neither necessary nor typical UI -- I do not remember any other UI which would ask to enter previously defined password twice just to make sure user entered it correctly.  Such double-entry is typically done on entry/when defining new passwords.  I think we should allow entry once, and if entered incorrectly, authentication would fail. and we should offer to reenter.  And I believe that is how it behaved before and would be after\n#2708 \nThoughts @mih since you are the one who introduced it -- what was your use case which shown the need in this verification?\n\nPS that code will be RFed slightly in the upcoming PR but I will retain the double entry as a default for now","files":null}]}